# Maximum Carnage in a game of two: a creature that can't attack a player other than Bot1 must still attack, and attacks
# Bot1 (the rulings). Bot2's Grizzly Bears, there before the Saga, may not stay home on Bot2's turn 4; Bot2's Memnite, cast
# that turn, can't attack (summoning sickness, CR 302.6), so it doesn't (the rulings). On Bot1's turn 5 the rule is over:
# chapter II's {R}{R}{R} comes with it, and Bot2's turn 6 needs no attack.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Maximum Carnage
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Grizzly Bears
Memnite
Island x16

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Maximum Carnage.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.LastingRules = Until your next turn, each creature attacks each combat if able and attacks a player other than you if able.
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
! Bot2.Attack()
! Bot2.Attack(Memnite > Bot1)
Bot2.Attack(Grizzly Bears > Bot1)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot1.Life = 18
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.LastingRules = (absent)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Mana = {R}{R}{R}
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack()
[T6 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Maximum Carnage.Counters.Lore = 2
